WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.902
Now we will combine several ideas into one small workflow.

00:00:03.902 --> 00:00:06.912
The input is a messy sales extract.

00:00:06.912 --> 00:00:11.622
First, we remove duplicate order IDs and create a copy.

00:00:11.622 --> 00:00:16.422
Then we standardize channel and status using strip and lower.

00:00:16.422 --> 00:00:23.852
Next, we clean the amount column by removing the dollar sign and converting the result to numeric values.

00:00:23.852 --> 00:00:29.292
We convert the date column to datetime and coerce invalid dates to missing values.

00:00:29.292 --> 00:00:34.732
Then we fill the missing city with Unknown and fill the missing amount using the median for this

00:00:34.732 --> 00:00:39.432
teaching example. Click Run and inspect the final DataFrame.

00:00:39.432 --> 00:00:42.562
The important lesson is the order of operations.

00:00:42.562 --> 00:00:45.902
We are not randomly applying Pandas functions.

00:00:45.902 --> 00:00:49.032
We are following a sequence that we can explain.

00:00:49.032 --> 00:00:55.577
Profile the data, understand the problems, convert types, standardize categories, handle missingness,

00:00:55.577 --> 00:00:58.582
remove true duplicates, and then inspect the result.

00:00:58.582 --> 00:01:05.722
In a production project, each decision would need to be justified more carefully,

00:01:05.722 --> 00:01:08.257
but this gives you a practical starting pattern.
